CURRENT candidate, which never appears in a frontier table, so the shipped
test does not compare a fractional base on the face against the same
candidate's frontier row. I probed it with a throwaway test (deleted) that
put base 7639.342517162467 on a SEARCHED (planned) candidate:
    frontier money: $7,639.34
    face line: … setting $7,639.34/mo · starting living budget $7,639.34/mo (the same at the start).
  i.e. the face and the frontier row agree at cents, no second formatter and
  no rounding drift. Evidence exists but is not pinned by a shipped test.

O2. The `<p data-spending-budget>` renders unconditionally (outside the
`{{if $row.MetricsAvailable}}` guard), and populateSpendingRowPlanEvidence's
only early return is `row == nil`, so no card can render an empty paragraph.
The criterion's fixture has metrics on all three candidates, so the
metrics-unavailable card is exercised only by the pre-existing
TestSpendingOptimizerRenderNilOrZeroSampleMetricsUnavailable (which passes);
no shipped assertion pins the budget line's presence on an Unavailable card.

O3. `make test` in the Makefile runs `go test ./...` without `-count=1`
(only the accounts package gets a forced re-run). I defeated the cache for
the package under test by running
`go test ./internal/handlers/whatif/ -count=1` separately, which is where the
evidence above comes from.

